    "['neighbor [parameter1] route-map [parameter2] [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set policy-options policy-statement policy1 then accept', 'parent_command': ['family inet unicast'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"neighbor route-map out\" command:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement policy1 then accept\\nset protocols bgp group EXTERNAL-PEER export policy1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command creates the policy statement (equivalent to Cisco\\'s route-map) with an accept action\\n2. The second command applies the policy as an export (outbound) policy to the BGP neighbor group\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would need to define the BGP neighbor under a group (here named \"EXTERNAL-PEER\") rather than directly like in Cisco. The actual neighbor IP would be configured within this group context.', 'trans_template': 'set policy-options policy-statement policy1 then accept'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols bgp group EXTERNAL-PEER export policy1', 'parent_command': ['family inet unicast'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"neighbor route-map out\" command:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement policy1 then accept\\nset protocols bgp group EXTERNAL-PEER export policy1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command creates the policy statement (equivalent to Cisco\\'s route-map) with an accept action\\n2. The second command applies the policy as an export (outbound) policy to the BGP neighbor group\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would need to define the BGP neighbor under a group (here named \"EXTERNAL-PEER\") rather than directly like in Cisco. The actual neighbor IP would be configured within this group context.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols bgp group EXTERNAL-PEER export policy1'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [parameter1] next-hop-self', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> neighbor 11.1.1.2 next-hop self', 'parent_command': ['family inet unicast'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `neighbor 11.1.1.2 next-hop-self` BGP command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols bgp group <group-name> neighbor 11.1.1.2 next-hop self\\n##\\n\\nNote: You'll need to replace `<group-name>` with the actual BGP group name used in your Juniper configuration, as Juniper requires BGP neighbors to be organized into groups. The group name isn't specified in the original Cisco configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> neighbor 11.1.1.2 next-hop self'}]]": 1,
